WEBVTT

00:03.850 --> 00:06.860
Anyone out there?
Answer if you're there!

00:08.980 --> 00:11.150
Why won't they respond?

00:11.150 --> 00:12.910
Maybe it's a ghost?

00:13.430 --> 00:17.120
They may not be in a condition to answer.

00:17.120 --> 00:20.080
But that could be seriously bad!

00:26.130 --> 00:27.210
Komiya!

00:30.100 --> 00:32.360
And Kinoshita from the same group.

00:33.090 --> 00:35.430
Hey, get up!

00:35.430 --> 00:37.980
Komiya, where's Shinohara?!

00:38.580 --> 00:41.060
It's no use. He's out cold.

00:41.400 --> 00:42.770
This one's out, too.

00:52.250 --> 00:56.240
<i>Shinohara wouldn't just leave them.</i>

00:56.660 --> 00:58.950
<i>Traces of third-party involvement...</i>

01:17.520 --> 01:23.320
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:21.370 --> 02:27.920
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:33.610 --> 02:35.780
No major external injuries.

02:35.780 --> 02:38.970
But what happens after
the teachers arrive?

02:35.890 --> 02:38.300
<b>#11 Connection</b>

02:38.970 --> 02:40.390
Whaddya mean?

02:40.700 --> 02:44.420
If they're deemed unable to continue,
they may have to drop out.

02:44.820 --> 02:48.640
If anything's happened to Shinohara,
all three will have to drop out,

02:49.200 --> 02:51.290
and they won't be able to avoid expulsion.

02:52.280 --> 02:53.750
Shinohara!

02:53.750 --> 02:54.490
Ike.

02:54.490 --> 02:56.230
I realize you're upset,

02:56.230 --> 03:00.240
but if she were seriously injured,
her alarm would be sounding.

03:00.940 --> 03:02.050
Yeah, but...

03:04.760 --> 03:06.540
Komiya! Can you hear me?

03:07.020 --> 03:08.110
Komiya!

03:08.110 --> 03:10.180
Ow! My leg...

03:12.260 --> 03:14.070
Oh, damn, your left leg...

03:14.820 --> 03:17.540
This may be the result of foul play.

03:17.920 --> 03:21.260
Komiya, do you remember the
circumstances under which you fell?

03:21.500 --> 03:26.480
No. I just felt this sudden
hit against my calf...

03:26.980 --> 03:29.270
Then I was tumbling downward...

03:29.600 --> 03:32.020
And Kinoshita was with you?

03:32.020 --> 03:33.500
Kinoshita?

03:34.080 --> 03:35.690
Yeah, I think...

03:36.580 --> 03:39.400
Oh, right! Where's Satsuki?!

03:39.630 --> 03:43.030
We don't know. She wasn't with you?

03:43.030 --> 03:45.410
Komiya! Where the hell is Shinohara?!

03:45.670 --> 03:47.410
I don't know!

03:47.820 --> 03:51.950
We were on the move when
Satsuki said she had to pee,

03:51.950 --> 03:55.400
so Kinoshita and I went
off to look down the slope.

03:55.400 --> 03:58.920
We were we discussing whether we
could use it as a shortcut, when...

03:58.920 --> 04:01.670
You felt the hit against your calf?

04:01.890 --> 04:06.810
Yeah. Then, the next thing
I knew, you guys were here.

04:08.680 --> 04:09.940
Shinohara!

04:10.610 --> 04:12.900
Hey, Kanji! Hang on!

04:13.690 --> 04:14.690
Senpai!

04:14.690 --> 04:15.860
Got it.

04:18.700 --> 04:21.690
Hey! Shinohara!

04:23.000 --> 04:25.280
Damn it. She's not here...

04:27.620 --> 04:29.830
Is that you, Ike?

04:30.290 --> 04:31.280
Shinohara?

04:32.160 --> 04:33.290
Shinohara!

04:37.150 --> 04:38.690
Have you been here the whole time?

04:38.690 --> 04:39.710
Yeah!

04:39.710 --> 04:44.470
Why didn't you call out earlier?!
Don't you know how worried I was?

04:44.900 --> 04:46.150
I just...

04:46.150 --> 04:49.180
I-I froze.

04:49.540 --> 04:50.740
I was so scared.

04:50.740 --> 04:51.850
I saw it...

04:51.850 --> 04:56.130
Someone pushed Komiya-kun and
Kinoshita-san down the slope...

04:56.130 --> 04:57.480
Who was it, though?!

04:57.480 --> 04:59.150
I don't know!

04:59.370 --> 05:00.820
I don't know... I just...

05:01.800 --> 05:03.420
Why did this happen?

05:05.080 --> 05:07.500
Let's meet back up with
the others for now.

05:07.980 --> 05:10.650
The teachers could be here any minute.

05:11.150 --> 05:12.910
R-Right.

05:14.790 --> 05:16.350
Hey, what's going on?

05:16.350 --> 05:18.970
Sudo-senpai, look after them.

05:18.970 --> 05:20.670
H-Hey!

05:23.940 --> 05:24.840
<i>{M}They're fast.</i>

05:26.800 --> 05:30.300
Wait! I just want to talk to you!

05:38.820 --> 05:41.640
Wait... Could she have...

05:48.710 --> 05:50.080
Where have you been?

05:50.080 --> 05:51.580
Something happen?

05:51.820 --> 05:52.670
No.

05:53.480 --> 05:57.710
More importantly, I'm glad
Shinohara-senpai was all right.

05:58.270 --> 06:01.590
It was too dark to see their face?

06:03.050 --> 06:05.180
But you saw the push?

06:05.180 --> 06:07.090
That's awfully convenient.

06:07.090 --> 06:09.670
Shinohara wouldn't lie!

06:09.670 --> 06:12.450
Testimony alone can't serve as proof.

06:12.450 --> 06:14.850
Then what's gonna happen to these two?!

06:14.850 --> 06:19.350
What do you think?
They're going to have to drop out.

06:19.570 --> 06:22.490
As their teacher, I'm not
thrilled about losing them,

06:22.490 --> 06:24.730
but they clearly can't continue.

06:25.090 --> 06:28.690
Shinohara-san could be lying to
cover up the self-inflicted injury,

06:28.690 --> 06:30.640
so that's what I have to assume.

06:30.640 --> 06:33.550
That's bullshit!
You can't do this to them!

06:33.980 --> 06:38.870
It's hopeless.
I can't do this by myself.

06:39.230 --> 06:41.630
Shinohara-san, what do you want to do?

06:41.980 --> 06:44.840
It won't be easy to continue on your own.

06:44.840 --> 06:49.200
You could avoid dropping out by
remaining near the starting point.

06:49.590 --> 06:52.510
You could at least do
challenges in the vicinity.

06:53.880 --> 06:55.120
Well, then, Shinohara-san,

06:55.120 --> 06:57.440
please make your way
back to the starting area.

06:57.820 --> 07:01.020
All right. I will.

07:07.870 --> 07:08.660
Ike!

07:16.900 --> 07:18.120
What now?

07:18.120 --> 07:20.640
Are you sure you're okay with this?

07:20.640 --> 07:26.780
I don't have a choice.
I can't survive this test on my own.

07:26.780 --> 07:29.050
But... But still...

07:29.050 --> 07:31.710
I'm getting expelled either way.

07:31.710 --> 07:33.050
Just let me go.

07:33.470 --> 07:36.310
I'll... I'll find a way to help you!

07:36.310 --> 07:37.930
Knock it off.

07:38.200 --> 07:40.200
It's totally hopeless.

07:40.200 --> 07:41.940
It's not hopeless, damn it!

07:41.940 --> 07:45.690
What's your problem?
It's not even your business.

07:45.690 --> 07:51.100
Besides, if I'm expelled, it lowers
the chance that you might be.

07:51.100 --> 07:52.450
You should celebrate.

07:52.450 --> 07:54.010
Celebrate?

07:54.010 --> 07:57.330
Don't be stupid.
I'd never celebrate that!

07:57.330 --> 07:58.830
Yeah?

07:59.300 --> 08:05.580
But what if you help me and it
drops your group to the bottom?

08:05.580 --> 08:08.210
You can't leave your guys
in the lurch like that.

08:08.210 --> 08:09.580
But...

08:10.150 --> 08:13.340
You never think this stuff through, Ike.

08:13.340 --> 08:16.560
It's gonna get you expelled
sooner or later.

08:16.920 --> 08:19.630
I'm gonna stay in the game
until the end no matter what,

08:20.040 --> 08:21.550
so give it your best, too.

08:22.740 --> 08:24.100
Wait a minute...

08:26.500 --> 08:28.260
I said wait!

08:29.110 --> 08:30.940
You're not done talking yet?!

08:31.230 --> 08:33.380
Yeah, not by a long shot.

08:33.940 --> 08:36.450
I don't want you to get expelled!

08:36.910 --> 08:38.430
That's why I wanna help!

08:42.590 --> 08:43.710
All right.

08:44.000 --> 08:47.780
Looks like it's time to
talk strats, Ryotaro.

08:47.780 --> 08:49.340
Y-Yeah!

08:50.650 --> 08:52.220
Chabashira-sensei.

08:52.220 --> 08:56.830
Could you look into something for
me back at the starting point?

08:56.830 --> 08:58.080
Confidentially.

09:01.080 --> 09:03.890
The best way to save Shinohara would be

09:03.890 --> 09:07.480
for her to join a group that's doing well.

09:07.700 --> 09:12.990
But would a group like that
really be willing to accept her?

09:13.340 --> 09:17.110
There's gotta be a way to
get her into another group.

09:17.420 --> 09:20.330
I do have a potential plan.

09:20.630 --> 09:21.950
What's it about?

09:22.170 --> 09:24.180
Unfortunately, it's far from certain.

09:24.180 --> 09:29.180
What we can do right now is have
Ike focused on protecting Shinohara,

09:29.180 --> 09:32.080
getting her as many game
points as possible.

09:33.760 --> 09:37.130
I'll begin making preparations
in case something happens.

09:37.850 --> 09:41.690
But if other students end up
in the bottom five groups,

09:41.690 --> 09:44.500
we may have to choose who we save.

09:44.950 --> 09:47.600
Bear that in mind, Ike.

09:48.850 --> 09:50.110
Got it.

09:50.110 --> 09:55.320
I may have to ignore designated
areas for a while.

09:55.320 --> 09:56.690
I'll still accompany you.

09:56.690 --> 10:00.490
To ignore those areas, you must be
going somewhere important, right?

10:00.850 --> 10:01.650
Yes.

10:08.410 --> 10:10.000
Oh, Senpai.

10:10.410 --> 10:12.140
Someone's fishing over there.

10:12.650 --> 10:18.150
<i>{M}One of the groups I was most
hoping to meet right now.</i>

10:20.360 --> 10:21.420
Are they biting?

10:21.750 --> 10:24.640
Unfortunately, no.

10:24.980 --> 10:29.020
The deserted island test is an
unexpected place for a date...

10:29.470 --> 10:30.840
Ayanokoji.

10:31.330 --> 10:34.400
I was just hoping to find you, Ryuen.

10:34.800 --> 10:38.830
I'm sure you've seen the report
about the bottom ten groups.

10:38.830 --> 10:44.580
Yeah. What's up with some of my
idiots being eighth on there?

10:44.580 --> 10:47.280
Komiya and Kinoshita have dropped out.

10:47.280 --> 10:50.170
Dropped out? What happened?

10:50.930 --> 10:52.520
What should we do, Ryuen?

10:52.870 --> 10:58.120
Even if we get into the top three,
it means nothing if we lose them.

10:58.540 --> 11:01.290
Shinohara's your classmate.

11:02.480 --> 11:05.790
Can I assume you have a plan
to keep them in the game?

11:09.830 --> 11:11.050
Got it.

11:11.690 --> 11:15.030
Yeah, that would keep Shinohara alive.

11:15.550 --> 11:18.620
But will it work?

11:18.970 --> 11:22.480
Your cooperation will certainly
make it more likely.

11:22.480 --> 11:25.660
I wouldn't hesitate to
cut bait on small fry,

11:26.240 --> 11:29.830
but Komiya and Kinoshita
are still useful to me.

11:30.610 --> 11:32.990
Can I consider this a deal?

11:33.740 --> 11:36.800
Your strategy is useful enough to me.

11:38.080 --> 11:42.220
If you run into Ichinose,
will you pass this on to her?

11:42.660 --> 11:45.440
Ichinose'll be a soft touch as usual,

11:45.870 --> 11:49.680
but I doubt Sakayanagi will
be so eager to cooperate.

11:57.650 --> 12:01.380
He got here quite early.

12:02.010 --> 12:04.230
That's Koenji Rokusuke.

12:04.790 --> 12:10.120
Koenji... He's from your class,
and currently in fourth place, right?

12:10.120 --> 12:13.620
He certainly has an aura about him.

12:15.400 --> 12:17.940
I'm dripping with charm from every pore!

12:18.570 --> 12:22.430
I seem to be even more
powerful than last year!

12:23.420 --> 12:27.360
He's saying something.
Is he talking to us?

12:27.360 --> 12:29.750
No, definitely to himself.

12:30.200 --> 12:32.800
He seems to be wallowing 
in his own self-regard.

12:33.220 --> 12:34.940
R-Right...

12:35.900 --> 12:39.530
It seems you're the one
I'll be competing with...

12:39.530 --> 12:41.160
Ayanokoji, my boy.

12:41.760 --> 12:43.280
True.

12:43.590 --> 12:47.700
<i>{M}My first one-on-one competition
is against Koenji...</i>

12:48.230 --> 12:51.940
<i>{M}I hope this isn't a sign of some
bizarre connection between us.</i>

12:53.270 --> 12:56.020
We'll start soon. Get ready.

12:56.710 --> 12:58.790
What's the matter, Senpai?

13:00.440 --> 13:04.550
I know you're a man who
prefers efficiency.

13:04.880 --> 13:07.300
I'm sure you've considered that

13:07.300 --> 13:10.680
it would be better to simply drop
out than to compete with me.

13:11.290 --> 13:15.990
You're the only person in Class 2-D
currently in the top ten groups.

13:16.460 --> 13:21.440
Stealing game points from each other
could be detrimental to both sides.

13:21.800 --> 13:24.190
I completely understand.

13:24.550 --> 13:29.210
Then let's cease the preamble
and begin, Ayanokoji, my boy.

13:30.580 --> 13:33.700
Three, two, one...

13:33.700 --> 13:34.630
Go!

13:40.540 --> 13:43.760
<i>{M}Is he waiting for me
to take this seriously?</i>

13:47.450 --> 13:50.530
To win, it is not technique you need...

13:50.920 --> 13:53.110
but power, plain and simple!

13:55.340 --> 13:57.410
<i>{M}We're evenly matched for strength.</i>

13:57.850 --> 14:02.130
<i>{M}His physical abilities really
are on another level.</i>

14:18.390 --> 14:22.670
You do like your efficiency.

14:23.950 --> 14:26.050
That's too bad, Senpai.

14:26.050 --> 14:31.640
Well, even if I'd gone all-out,
it wouldn't have been much of a match.

14:32.400 --> 14:34.080
How are you holding up?

14:34.080 --> 14:35.030
I'm all right.

14:35.680 --> 14:37.370
Let's push on ahead, then.

14:37.790 --> 14:38.560
Right.

14:45.820 --> 14:47.950
Senpai, look.

14:49.380 --> 14:51.390
Isn't that Koenji-senpai again?

14:52.330 --> 14:56.790
<i>{M}I'm sure he didn't just start this way
after the challenge was announced...</i>

14:57.500 --> 14:58.850
<i>{M}But it's a surprise.</i>

15:01.070 --> 15:06.130
I'm very sorry. The last of the boy
slots filled up a few minutes ago.

15:06.410 --> 15:07.550
I see.

15:08.230 --> 15:09.130
What will you do?

15:09.450 --> 15:13.140
I'm not in my best shape, but I'd
rather not waste the opportunity.

15:13.580 --> 15:16.160
All right. I'll wait over there.

15:16.500 --> 15:17.240
Right.

15:21.210 --> 15:22.430
Sakayanagi.

15:23.720 --> 15:25.820
Good day to you, Ayanokoji-kun.

15:25.820 --> 15:28.840
It's going to be another
hot day, isn't it?

15:29.460 --> 15:30.400
How are you doing?

15:31.100 --> 15:33.420
Well enough, I suppose.

15:34.140 --> 15:36.980
Now, may I ask what brings you here today?

15:37.440 --> 15:41.090
I wanted to ask you for a favor.

15:42.040 --> 15:44.920
Have you heard that Komiya and
Kinoshita had to drop out?

15:45.160 --> 15:49.880
Yes, and Shinohara-san
is still in the fight.

15:49.880 --> 15:53.170
Can I assume that someone is helping her?

15:53.520 --> 15:55.030
That's correct.

15:55.030 --> 15:59.260
But maintaining a solo fight in the
test's latter half won't be easy.

16:00.050 --> 16:04.430
I'm sure you'd like to see her
absorbed by another group soon.

16:04.940 --> 16:09.180
I see. And that's why you want my help?

16:09.550 --> 16:11.950
Have you met with Ryuen-kun?

16:12.460 --> 16:14.850
Yes, and he agreed to my plan.

16:15.710 --> 16:19.200
He seems to think highly
of Komiya and Kinoshita.

16:19.450 --> 16:22.770
But unlike him, I have nothing
to gain by helping you.

16:22.770 --> 16:26.680
If it doesn't affect Class A, 
I have no reason to care.

16:27.530 --> 16:32.220
Though if you would agree to help
me under the same conditions,

16:32.630 --> 16:34.400
I may reconsider.

16:35.190 --> 16:36.720
I accept.

16:37.380 --> 16:40.950
Or so I'd like to say,
but we'll need more people first.

16:41.920 --> 16:43.480
I'll contact you later.

16:43.480 --> 16:46.040
I'll leave the networking in your hands.

16:49.180 --> 16:50.230
Hello.

16:50.460 --> 16:51.760
Ayanokoji?

16:52.390 --> 16:54.230
Browse the stock as you listen to me.

16:54.670 --> 16:57.490
About the actions of
Acting Chairman Tsukishiro...

16:58.290 --> 17:01.250
To deal with emergencies that
may arise during the test,

17:01.250 --> 17:05.360
we have a helicopter and a boat on call.

17:05.360 --> 17:07.750
But for some reason,
there are two boats this time.

17:07.750 --> 17:12.260
<b>Spring Water                         Energy Bar                          Canned Salmon</b>

17:07.750 --> 17:12.260
<b>Combat Rations                         Canned Fruit                             Canned Yakitori</b>

17:07.750 --> 17:12.260
<b>Gas Burner                                 Spoon                                        Fork</b>

17:07.750 --> 17:12.260
<b>Knife                                     Lantern                                  Sleeping Bag</b>

17:08.050 --> 17:12.260
I looked into it, and this was apparently
arranged on Tsukishiro's orders.

17:12.520 --> 17:14.510
Where is the acting chairman now?

17:14.980 --> 17:17.970
He generally stays in the staff
facility's observation room,

17:18.290 --> 17:20.550
watching for abnormalities in the watches.

17:21.480 --> 17:23.980
But several times a day,
he goes out on patrol.

17:24.440 --> 17:26.460
Personally? By himself?

17:26.460 --> 17:27.630
Yes.

17:27.630 --> 17:29.630
I certainly have a bad feeling about this.

17:30.040 --> 17:31.790
Be careful, Ayanokoji.

17:32.230 --> 17:34.830
I appreciate the warning.

17:41.050 --> 17:43.910
Onodera from our class took first.

17:43.910 --> 17:46.240
She's a tough one to beat in swimming.

17:46.900 --> 17:48.540
Don't let it bother you.

17:48.880 --> 17:51.800
True, Onodera-senpai was impressive.

17:51.800 --> 17:54.800
But the one that really
caught my attention...

17:53.170 --> 17:54.800
Perfect!

17:55.090 --> 17:57.180
He's an anomaly,
in every sense of the word.

17:57.610 --> 17:59.600
Worrying about him is a waste of time.

18:01.450 --> 18:06.500
<i>The reward from this will push him
to number one in the rankings.</i>

18:06.830 --> 18:09.080
<i>He's truly a man of immeasurable ability.</i>

18:13.210 --> 18:15.440
I'm getting thirsty.

18:15.970 --> 18:19.470
It's nice to refresh
at the starting point,

18:19.900 --> 18:22.450
but it also makes you crave water more.

18:22.840 --> 18:26.450
Is that why so many groups were there?

18:26.740 --> 18:28.270
Not just that.

18:28.270 --> 18:31.960
The main reason was to see
the bottom ten groups.

18:32.310 --> 18:35.280
Only the bottom five groups
are at risk of expulsion.

18:35.610 --> 18:39.850
Having that information starting
on Day 4 gives you room to breathe.

18:39.850 --> 18:42.460
Even if you've decided to
fight at full strength,

18:42.460 --> 18:44.580
reality is rarely so accommodating.

18:45.240 --> 18:49.490
It's important to rest at some times,
and push past your limits at others.

18:49.850 --> 18:53.970
The question is when you do each one.

18:54.730 --> 19:00.890
You seem to have actively avoided
peaking in the first half.

19:01.960 --> 19:04.130
That's my general policy.

19:04.130 --> 19:06.700
If a chance presents itself,
I'll push myself past my limit,

19:06.700 --> 19:10.280
but throwing my all into
highly competitive challenges

19:10.280 --> 19:12.170
won't earn many game points.

19:12.170 --> 19:15.600
Um, why are you telling me all this?

19:15.600 --> 19:17.730
You're clearly my enemy.

19:18.550 --> 19:22.140
That's partly because this test is a
competition with other grade years,

19:22.380 --> 19:25.850
but there's also a test
about having me expelled.

19:26.870 --> 19:28.140
True...

19:28.850 --> 19:32.150
But another part of me thinks
you aren't actually my enemy.

19:33.710 --> 19:35.020
Isn't that strange?

19:51.960 --> 19:53.000
Grab on.

20:04.070 --> 20:07.470
Senpai, do you enjoy your
time at this school?

20:07.790 --> 20:12.090
It's frequently difficult,
but I've never found it unenjoyable.

20:12.770 --> 20:17.070
I would like to make it to
graduation without regrets.

20:17.630 --> 20:18.890
Graduation...

20:20.180 --> 20:21.320
What's the matter?

20:22.520 --> 20:23.390
I...

20:25.610 --> 20:26.970
It's nothing.

20:32.480 --> 20:33.580
Tsubaki-san.

20:33.830 --> 20:35.530
Could we talk?

20:35.890 --> 20:36.960
What is it?

20:37.180 --> 20:40.340
You're planning something big, aren't you?

20:41.070 --> 20:46.590
Expelling Ayanokoji-senpai
will get us 20 million points.

20:46.930 --> 20:49.470
Anyone would find that appealing.

20:50.110 --> 20:55.300
Refusing to play along could get
you in a whole lot of trouble.

20:55.300 --> 20:56.480
Trouble?

20:56.700 --> 20:59.980
Someone who matters to you
could end up in danger.

21:00.310 --> 21:01.730
Or something like that.

21:01.730 --> 21:03.820
You mean Kushida-senpai?

21:03.820 --> 21:06.140
What about Kushida-senpai?

21:06.600 --> 21:08.830
Why do you care so much about her?

21:08.830 --> 21:10.490
N-No reason.

21:10.490 --> 21:14.330
I'm sorry, but I don't
have anything to tell—

21:16.020 --> 21:20.100
What are you doing, Utomiya-kun?!

21:20.780 --> 21:23.190
I have nothing against you,

21:23.190 --> 21:25.470
but you can either tell
me what I want to know,

21:25.860 --> 21:27.980
or drop out right here.

21:27.980 --> 21:29.470
It's one or the other.

21:29.720 --> 21:34.680
I've determined that Kushida-senpai
is an important part of your plan.

21:35.230 --> 21:37.000
Why is that?

21:37.610 --> 21:38.900
I won't tell you.

21:40.960 --> 21:42.860
The cat's out of the bag, though.

21:43.370 --> 21:47.240
If you don't tell us,
we'll just ask her personally.

21:47.640 --> 21:50.140
Will you tell us or not?

21:51.190 --> 21:52.990
F-Fine...

21:53.600 --> 21:56.750
I'll tell you... everything.
